##
##    PrePoMax --> code_aster from "pmx2aster.py" V0.1.4 | [ 01-Oct-2025 ] 
##    Made by Sound Spinning | soundspinning@hotmail.com
##    Meant to be run from a terminal with `run_aster *.export` instead of with `as_run`
##

 #  "forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.inp" model HEADING:
 # Hash: xfrezGit, Date: 10/28/2025, Unit system: MM_TON_S_C
 # # forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.pmx
 # # 2-cube assembly + (soft) couplings + TIED contact constraint
 # # ------------------------------------------------------------
 # # Forced response (Modal Dynamics - shock wave) as a restart from modal results
 # ---------------------------------
 # 

### RAM in MB - Since V16.7 the solver grabs 90% of this input
P memory_limit 64000
P ncpus 1
### max solve time in seconds ==> 4e5s = 4.63days 
P time_limit 400000.0

## Input deck
F comm forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.comm D  1

## Input mesh - ASTER format
F mesh forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.msh D  21

## Output message file
F mesg forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.msg R  6

## Output text results file
F data forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.dat R  8

## MED results file#1
F rmed forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes.rmed R  80
## MED results file#2
F rmed forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes_points_springs.rmed R  81

## Output FOLDER for global restart files, also useful for Sub-modelling
## When reading the `base` in a restart run, change RC --> DC
## R base forced_global_R3_coups_2_cubes RC 0

## Output local temp FOLDER (if needed) for solver temp (.med) files
## R repe TMP R  0

## RESTART reads global results folder
R base global_R3_coups_2_cubes DC 0
